<title>POLAND: Polish budget deficit up to PLN 7.48 bln in June.</title>
<headline>Polish budget deficit up to PLN 7.48 bln in June.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish budget deficit widened by 900 million to 7.48 billion zlotys in June, which accounted for 61.2 percent of the planned 1997 deficit of 12.22 billion zlotys, the finance ministry said.  </p>
<p> POLISH BUDGET GAP	Jan-June	Jan-May    1997 plan</p>
<p> balance in bln PLN	 7.48	    6.58	 12.220</p>
<p> revenue		     50.56	   40.71	115.334</p>
<p> expenditure		 58.04	   47.29	127.554</p>
<p>NOTE: Jan-May figures given as reported last month.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
